πτῶμα -τος, τό
(πίπτω), [in LXX: Jdg.14.8 (מַפֶּלֶת), Job.16.15 (14) (פֶּרֶץ), Isa.51.19 (שֹׁד), Jdt.8.19, Wis.4.18, al. ;] 
__1. a fall, metaphorically, a misfortune, calamity (Trag., Plat., Polyb., al.; LXX). 
__2. That which has fallen; 
__(a) of buildings, a ruin (Polyb.); 
__(b) of living creatures, in cl. (poët. only) usually with genitive, νεκρῶν, etc., but also absol., as in late writers and NT, a fallen…
